+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "### Displaying the vector cells with respect to the `Agent`\n",
+    "We can use the vector cell function `.display_vector_cells()` to visualise the vector cells in the environment and their firing rates with respect to the position of the agent. \n",
+    "\n",
+    "This can be used to make nice animations. In the following you'll see how the position of each little oval represents the tuning of each vector cell (corroborate these with the OVC rate maps above) and its firing rate is represented by the color. This should increase whenever it cross the object type / boundary it is selective for. This oval is an approximation to the full distribution of the vector cell's tuning curve (this is a Gaussian in distance x a von mises in angle).\n",
+    "\n",
+    "In this case we'll visualise the `BoundaryVectorCells` so notice how the firing rate increases when the agent approaches a the boundary at the correct angle."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 13,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
