+   "source": [
+    "### Ego- and Allocentric \n",
+    "\n",
+    "By default vector cells are allocentric. This means their angular tuning is repect to due-North. However, it is possible to make them egocentric, i.e. their angular tuning is relative to the animal's head direction. This is done by setting the the `'reference_frame'` parameter to `'egocentric'`. \n",
+    "\n",
+    "Since these cells now depend on head direction we may optinally like to smooth the head direction (head direction = velocity smoothed with a decaying expontial kernel), as done here. "
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 15,
